{{/* Codex reads ~/.codex/AGENTS.md now. ~/AGENTS.md was a stale copy that
     Claude Code also loads as project rules anywhere under ~, and it says it
     wins on conflict. The pattern matches only the file at the top of ~. */}}
AGENTS.md

{{/* Codex runs no review gates, so its unmanaged copies of the Claude agents
     only drift. chezmoi deletes whatever this glob matches on every apply on
     every machine, so any future ~/.codex/agents/*.toml goes too, by design.
     A directory named *.toml goes with its contents. If ~/.codex/agents is a
     symlink, chezmoi follows it and deletes the .toml files in its target. */}}
.codex/agents/*.toml

{{/* launchd runs the scheduled jobs now (Library/LaunchAgents); the crontab
     file they replaced has no reader left. */}}
.cron/crontab

